t for `deviceEnrol`."},"client":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EnrolClient","description":"For `deviceEnrol` only, and then REQUIRED: the client the request names, as auth/oob/request/0.3 carried it. Self-asserted by the client."},"requestedScope":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RequestedScope","description":"For `deviceEnrol` only, and then REQUIRED: the ceiling the request asks for, as auth/oob/request/0.3 carried it, unchanged. The grant chooses within it."},"ext":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Ext"}},"oneOf":[{"properties":{"purpose":{"const":"login","description":"Selects the `login` shape."}},"not":{"anyOf":[{"required":["client"]},{"required":["requestedScope"]}]}},{"properties":{"purpose":{"const":"deviceEnrol","description":"Selects the `deviceEnrol` shape."}},"required":["client","requestedScope"],"not":{"required":["signingScope"]}}]},"Ext":{"title":"Ext","description":"Vendor-namespaced extension object per SPEC.md §4.5.1. Each immediate key MUST be a reverse-DNS namespace; structure under each namespace is opaque to the framework.","type":"object","minProperties":1,"additionalProperties":true,"propertyNames":{"pattern":"^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*(\\\\.[a-z0-9-]+)+\$"}},"RequestedScope":{"title":"RequestedScope","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["capabilities","purposes","keys","maxLifetimeDays"],"properties":{"capabilities":{"type":"array","maxItems":32,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/CapabilityRef"},"description":"The most capabilities the client asks to hold, in the VTA\'s capability registry. Empty asks for none. A grant may hold these or fewer, never others."},"purposes":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/PurposeScope","description":"The most purposes the client asks to use content it reads for. A grant may name these or fewer; `any` here lets the approver choose any purpose except `modelTraining`, which is granted only by naming it. A wallet shows `any` to the person as any purpose (CONVENTIONS.md §7 A14)."},"keys":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/KeyScope","description":"The most keys the client asks to invoke the VTA\'s signing oracle on: `none`, or `listed`. Never `all` for `deviceEnrol` (CONVENTIONS.md §7 A14). A grant may name these or fewer."},"maxLifetimeDays":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":365,"description":"The longest the client asks the enrolment to last, in days from the grant\'s `issuedAt`. The grant\'s `aclScope.expiresAt` may be earlier, never later. There is no unbounded enrolment."}},"not":{"properties":{"keys":{"properties":{"scope":{"const":"all"}},"required":["scope"]}},"required":["keys"]},"description":"The ceiling a client asks to be enrolled under, stated in an auth/oob/request for `deviceEnrol` and repeated in step 2. It is a ceiling, not a grant: the approver chooses the scope (`AclScope`) and the service refuses a grant that exceeds this. Where the client may act (the contexts) is not part of the ceiling; the approver chooses it."},"KeyScope":{"title":"KeyScope","description":"An explicit key scope. Exactly one of three shapes, discriminated by `scope`: `all`, `none`, or `listed` with a NON-EMPTY list of key identifiers. The empty list is invalid, not a fourth shape.","oneOf":[{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/KeyScopeAll"},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/KeyScopeNone"},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/KeyScopeListed"}]},"KeyScopeListed":{"title":"KeyScopeListed","description":"Exactly the listed keys, intersected with the entry\'s act scope.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["scope","keys"],"properties":{"scope":{"const":"listed"},"keys":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":512},"description":"Non-empty set of key identifiers. An empty array is invalid (it is neither `all` nor `none`)."}}},"KeyScopeNone":{"title":"KeyScopeNone","description":"No keys.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["scope"],"properties":{"scope":{"const":"none"}}},"KeyScopeAll":{"title":"KeyScopeAll","description":"Every key the entry\'s act scope reaches.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["scope"],"properties":{"scope":{"const":"all"}}},"PurposeScope":{"title":"PurposeScope","description":"An explicit purpose scope. Exactly one of two shapes, discriminated by `scope`: `any`, or `listed` with a NON-EMPTY list of purposes. The empty list is invalid, not a third shape.","oneOf":[{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/PurposeScopeAny"},{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/PurposeScopeListed"}]},"PurposeScopeListed":{"title":"PurposeScopeListed","description":"Exactly the listed purposes. A request naming any other purpose is refused.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["scope","purposes"],"properties":{"scope":{"const":"listed"},"purposes":{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":32,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Purpose"},"description":"Non-empty set of purposes. An empty array is invalid (it is not `any`)."}}},"Purpose":{"title":"Purpose","description":"What content is used for: a lowerCamelCase name registered in the VTI specification\'s purpose registry (Appendix H) — `personalisation`, `taskExecution`, `analytics`, `modelTraining` at the time of writing — or an absolute IRI naming a purpose defined elsewhere, such as a purpose of the W3C Data Privacy Vocabulary (`https://w3id.org/dpv#ServicePersonalisation`). Compared by exact string equality: a consumer MUST NOT treat a purpose it does not recognise as equal to any other, and grants only a request naming exactly a listed purpose (VTI-ACL-109). A registered name is never an IRI, because it contains no `:`.","type":"string","maxLength":2048,"anyOf":[{"pattern":"^[a-z][a-zA-Z0-9]{0,63}\$"},{"pattern":"^[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9+.-]*:[^\\\\s]+\$"}]},"PurposeScopeAny":{"title":"PurposeScopeAny","description":"Any purpose except `modelTraining` (training, fine-tuning or evaluating a machine-learning model on the content), which `any` never grants (VTI-ACL-105).","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["scope"],"properties":{"scope":{"const":"any"}}},"CapabilityRef":{"title":"CapabilityRef","description":"A capability, optionally qualified by a resource. Used where a capability is named but not granted — a role\'s ceiling, a role\'s approve ceiling, an entry\'s approvable capabilities. An unqualified reference covers every resource of the capability\'s kind.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["capability"],"properties":{"capability":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/Capability"},"resource":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/ResourceQualifier","description":"Optional qualifier. Absent covers every resource of the capability\'s kind."}}},"ResourceQualifier":{"title":"ResourceQualifier","description":"Opaque qualifier naming the part of the maintainer\'s resources a capability applies to (e.g. `git-ns:github.com/acme`, `git-repo:github.com/acme/r#4211`, `policy:join`). Its grammar and containment rule are the maintainer\'s: a qualified capability covers the named resource and the resources inside it. A qualifier MUST NOT be read as widening the entry\'s act scope.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":512},"Capability":{"title":"Capability","description":"Opaque identifier of one administrative power in the maintainer\'s capability registry — lowercase dot-separated segments (e.g. `keys.sign`, `vtc.roles.assign`, `git.repo.manage`). A consumer MUST NOT treat a capability it does not recognise as granted.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":128,"pattern":"^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*(\\\\.[a-z0-9-]+)*\$"},"EnrolClient":{"title":"EnrolClient","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["consumerKind","displayName"],"properties":{"consumerKind":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/ConsumerKind","description":"What kind of client asks to be enrolled, in the device family\'s own terms: a `companion` (`browser`, `mobile`, `desktop`) or a `service` (`mediator`, `aiAgent`, `daemon`). Self-asserted by the starter. The grant repeats it, and the VTA holds it beside the ACL entry the enrolment creates (CONVENTIONS §7 A9)."},"displayName":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64,"description":"The name the client gives itself (e.g. `Research agent on laptop`). Self-asserted and untrusted wherever rendered: an approver shows it as the client\'s own claim, never as a name the service vouches for."}},"description":"Who asks to be enrolled, as the client states it in an auth/oob/request for `deviceEnrol`. Revealed only in step 2, to the lock holder, after an admin identity and number proof."},"ConsumerKind":{"title":"ConsumerKind","description":"Discriminator: is this consumer a user-driven Companion or a headless Service?","oneOf":[{"title":"Companion","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["kind","formFactor"],"properties":{"kind":{"const":"companion"},"formFactor":{"type":"string","enum":["browser","mobile","desktop"]}}},{"title":"Service","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["kind","serviceKind"],"properties":{"kind":{"const":"service"},"serviceKind":{"type":"string","enum":["mediator","aiAgent","daemon"]}}}]},"SigningScope":{"title":"SigningScope","type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":8,"uniqueItems":true,"items":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/TaskFamily"},"description":"The task families a `login` grant lets the starter key sign documents for, as the approving DID, for the session the grant arms (auth/oob/grant/0.2). Offered by the service in step 2, copied unchanged into the grant, and bounded further by the exclusions auth/oob/grant/0.2 states. Absent means the starter key signs nothing beyond the family\'s own tasks."},"TaskFamily":{"title":"TaskFamily","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":128,"pattern":"^[a-z][a-z0-9]*(-[a-z0-9]+)*(/[a-z][a-z0-9]*(-[a-z0-9]+)*)*\$","description":"A family of Trust Tasks, named by a slug prefix of whole segments (SPEC §6.1 grammar): `vtc/directory` names every task whose slug is `vtc/directory` or begins `vtc/directory/`, at any version. A prefix matches on segment boundaries only, so `vtc/dir` names nothing under `vtc/directory`."},"Requester":{"title":"Requester","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["location","browser","os","createdAt","sameNetwork"],"properties":{"location":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":128,"description":"City and country of the starter\'s connection, from a local lookup with no third-party call, or the literal `unknown`. Never an IP address."},"browser":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64,"description":"Browser family of the starter (e.g. `Chrome`), never the full User-Agent; `unknown` when it cannot be told."},"os":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64,"description":"Operating system family of the starter (e.g. `macOS`); `unknown` when it cannot be told."},"createdAt":{"type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"When the service accepted the starter\'s auth/oob/request."},"sameNetwork":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/SameNetwork"}},"description":"What the service reports about where the request came from. Revealed only in the step 2 response, to the lock holder, after a membership and number proof. Reported by the service, signed by it, and a heuristic: a relaying attacker controls what is observed."},"SameNetwork":{"title":"SameNetwork","oneOf":[{"type":"boolean"},{"type":"string","const":"unknown"}],"description":"Whether the starter\'s request and the approver\'s prove came from the same egress network, as the service saw them: `true`, `false`, or the string `unknown` when the service cannot tell. The service compares addresses; it never discloses them."},"OobKey":{"title":"OobKey","type":"string","minLength":48,"maxLength":64,"pattern":"^did:key:z6Mk[1-9A-HJ-NP-Za-km-z]+\$","description":"A starter key (`K_b`) or an approver lock key (`K_a`), as an Ed25519 `did:key` (`z6Mk…`) generated for this one request and used nowhere else. Ed25519 only: a service refuses any other key type with `auth/oob:keyUnsupported` before parsing beyond the multicodec prefix."},"OobPurpose":{"title":"OobPurpose","type":"string","enum":["login","deviceEnrol"],"description":"What the request is for. A CLOSED list: each purpose has a fixed row in CONVENTIONS.md §3 stating what is revealed at each step, what the grant contains, what redeem returns and the window lengths. Version 0.2 defines `login` and `deviceEnrol`; version 0.1 defined `login` only. `stepUp` is a reserved name; adding a purpose is a new version of this component and of every task that references it, never an in-place edit. Named `OobPurpose` from 0.2, where 0.1 named it `Purpose`, so that it cannot be confused with the ACL family\'s `Purpose` (what content is used for), which the 0.2 scope records reference; the values on the wire are unchanged."},"Origin":{"title":"Origin","type":"string","minLength":9,"maxLength":2048,"pattern":"^https://[^/?#\\\\s]+\$","description":"A web origin (`https://host[:port]`, no path, no trailing slash). For `login`, the origin of the portal where the starter runs, which is the origin of the `serviceEndpoint` of the service\'s `SignInPortal` service in its DID document. For `deviceEnrol`, the origin of the `serviceEndpoint` of the service\'s `TrustTaskHTTPS` service in its DID document: the VTA endpoint the starter opened the request at."},"Service":{"title":"Service","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["did","name"],"properties":{"did":{"type":"string","pattern":"^did:","minLength":5,"maxLength":2048,"description":"The service\'s DID: the `recipient` of every request in the family, and the `_from` of the trigger link. For `deviceEnrol`, the DID of the VTA the client is enrolled at."},"name":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":128,"description":"The name the service calls itself. Supplied by the service: an approver shows the name from its OWN records and flags a difference from this one (VTI-LNK-104); it never shows this value as the community\'s name on its own authority."}},"description":"Who the service says it is."},"RequestId":{"title":"RequestId","type":"string","minLength":22,"maxLength":43,"pattern":"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{22,43}\$","description":"The service-generated handle of one request: 16 to 32 bytes from a cryptographically secure random source, written as unpadded base64url (22 to 43 characters; 16 bytes, 22 characters, is RECOMMENDED). It is also the nonce of the exchange, so the family needs no separate challenge, and it is the `_id` of the trigger link (VTI-LNK-033). Compared as a string. It confers no authority on its holder."}}}';

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the request variant, taken from this
/// specification's front matter.
///
/// Pass it to [consumeInbound] — items 5b, 7 and 8 are per-specification and
/// cannot be derived from the document alone, and item 2 needs the schema it
/// carries.
const SpecPolicy spec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: typeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: true,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: true,
  payloadSchema: payloadSchemaJson,
);

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the success-response variant.
///
/// `isRecipientRequired` tracks the *issuer* party's requirement, because a
/// response swaps the parties (§7.3 item 5).
const SpecPolicy responseSpec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: responseTypeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: true,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: true,
  payloadSchema: responsePayloadSchemaJson,
);
